   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Guessing about the present",
     "texto": [
      "To describe a present state, adjectives use **-(으)ㄴ 것 같아요**: 피곤하다 → **피곤한 것 같아요** (seems/I think they are tired), 비싸다 → **비싼 것 같아요** (seems expensive). Verbs use **-는 것 같아요**: 자다 → **자는 것 같아요** (seems they sleep). **것 같아요** expresses an impression or judgement; it can be based on what you see, or on other information."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Time contrast",
     "texto": [
      "For a guess about a past state, use **-았/었던 것 같아요**: 피곤했었던 것 같아요 (I think they were tired). For a past action, forms such as **잤던 것 같아요** (I think they slept) are possible; past forms can vary depending on aspect and context. For a future or not yet realised possibility, use **-(으)ㄹ 것 같아요**, as in the previous lesson. Here we focus on the basic present/past/future contrast."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
